msgid ""
"Home shows whether updates are found and installed. The thorough check here "
"goes further.\n"
"\n"
"Every program installed from a package comes with a list of its files and a "
"checksum for each. This check reads every one of those files and compares it "
"with its checksum, so a changed or missing file shows up, whether a person, "
"a program or malware changed it. Your own settings in /etc are not counted: "
"changing them is normal.\n"
"\n"
"It reads tens of thousands of files and can take from half a minute to "
"several minutes. Reading all of them needs the administrator password. "
"gAudit only reads; it changes nothing.\n"
"\n"
"A clean result means no changes were found, not that the computer is proven "
"clean: the checksums are not signed once installed, so someone with full "
"control of the computer could change them too."
msgstr ""

